WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:23.760
Well, trail heard delivered, top price for our beef.

00:23.760 --> 00:25.180
Beautiful San Francisco weather.

00:25.180 --> 00:26.180
What more could we ask?

00:26.180 --> 00:27.180
Well, a few days out of the saddle.

00:27.180 --> 00:28.180
By God, we'll have that, too.

00:28.180 --> 00:33.080
Listen, as a change from Hop Sink's chuck wagon, I'm throwing a little supper party

00:33.080 --> 00:34.080
tonight.

00:34.080 --> 00:35.080
Oysters, steak, champagne, the works.

00:35.080 --> 00:40.120
After that, after that, five days for all of us in San Francisco with nothing to do

00:40.120 --> 00:41.120
but have a good time.

00:41.120 --> 00:42.120
Hey, there's the deal.

00:42.120 --> 00:43.120
Oh, that's what I've been waiting to hear you say.

00:43.120 --> 00:44.120
What's the matter, Johnny?

00:44.120 --> 00:48.000
Well, Mr. Cartwright, I think you made a mistake here.

00:48.000 --> 00:49.000
I got too much pay.

00:49.000 --> 00:50.000
Oh, no, you haven't.

00:50.000 --> 00:51.000
You and Ham both deserve a bonus.

00:51.000 --> 00:56.880
Now, you're going to have a good time, but remember, this is not the Ponderosa in San

00:56.880 --> 00:57.880
Francisco, so be careful.

00:57.880 --> 01:01.040
Thanks, boss, but don't worry about us.

01:01.040 --> 01:05.240
After riding trail with these boys of yours, this town is going to seem downright tame.

01:05.240 --> 01:06.240
Thanks a lot.

01:06.240 --> 01:07.240
Come on, Ham.

01:07.240 --> 01:08.240
Don't be late for supper.

01:08.240 --> 01:09.240
Fine boys.

01:09.240 --> 01:16.240
Now, with hands like Johnny and Ham, we won't have any trouble running the Ponderosa.

01:16.240 --> 01:21.240
Well, let's get back to the hotel.

01:21.240 --> 01:24.240
This isn't fun.

01:24.240 --> 01:29.480
Ham, I'm beginning to like this San Francisco town.

01:29.480 --> 01:31.440
You know something?

01:31.440 --> 01:32.800
You know what I'm going to do?

01:32.800 --> 01:37.480
I'm going to buy that sweet wife of mine a whole bowl of Chinese silk.

01:37.480 --> 01:38.480
Silk?

01:38.480 --> 01:39.800
You say silk?

01:39.800 --> 01:42.040
I said silk.

01:42.040 --> 01:44.320
Nothing too good for that sweet wife of mine.

01:44.320 --> 01:46.480
Gentlemen, I just happened to overhear.

01:46.480 --> 01:52.160
Now, as you see by my card, I'm a silk merchant, and I just happened to have a brand new shipment

01:52.160 --> 01:53.160
from the Oriole.

01:53.160 --> 01:54.720
It's the home of the silkworm.

01:54.720 --> 01:56.920
Now, if you'll follow me to my establishment...

01:56.920 --> 01:57.920
Why, sure, neighbor.

01:57.920 --> 02:02.920
Yes, gentlemen, right back here.

02:02.920 --> 02:15.680
I have my shop because it's wholesale.

02:15.680 --> 02:20.000
Right this way, gentlemen.

02:20.000 --> 02:24.320
I hope Shanghai Pete takes them off my hands that ship sails for Hong Kong at midnight.

02:24.320 --> 02:25.320
Pick them in, boys.

02:25.320 --> 02:54.440
I better leave in aawk for 60 minutes to make my way there.

02:54.440 --> 03:01.440
That's very strange. Johnny and Ab should be here by now.

03:03.600 --> 03:05.520
Don't worry about them two, Paul. They'll be here.

03:05.520 --> 03:09.680
They ain't gonna turn down free horses and champagne, I'll guarantee you.

03:09.680 --> 03:12.320
He's right, bud.

03:12.320 --> 03:14.520
Hey, I was gonna get laid.

03:14.520 --> 03:15.400
Oh?

03:15.400 --> 03:16.240
What?

03:16.240 --> 03:18.040
I didn't know that.

03:18.040 --> 03:19.400
Adam sells a big tub.

03:19.400 --> 03:21.800
Adam's working himself to death.

03:21.800 --> 03:24.720
Yeah, dog gone with that too, Paul.

03:24.720 --> 03:31.720
Well, it's too bad you boys didn't think about that before you reaped those straws you drew to see who'd come on this trip.

03:34.520 --> 03:36.320
What about Hop Sings? He gonna come along?

03:36.320 --> 03:41.120
Oh, I doubt that very much. He's got a hundred relatives in town he wants to visit.

03:41.120 --> 03:43.760
We sure will have a job here when we get back.

03:43.760 --> 03:48.960
After summer, me and little Joe's gonna figure out a place where they got them good-looking waiter gals.

03:48.960 --> 03:52.240
Ha ha, you talking, brother?

03:52.240 --> 03:58.120
If you think I'm gonna let you and little Joe wander around the Barbary Coast at night alone, you've got yourself another thing coming.

03:58.120 --> 04:00.880
This is San Francisco. It's a big city, and it's a wild city.

04:00.880 --> 04:02.680
Yeah, but, Paul, you're not Hampton Johnny, though.

04:02.680 --> 04:04.640
Well, you're not Hampton Johnny.

04:04.640 --> 04:06.360
Have you ever heard of Shanghai?

04:06.360 --> 04:07.960
Yeah, it's got something to do with sailors, doesn't it?

04:07.960 --> 04:10.280
You know there isn't a ship in this harbor that isn't short of sailors.

04:10.280 --> 04:14.280
You could be slugged over the head and on your way to Singapore before you even knew what happened.

04:14.280 --> 04:15.960
That's a different thing.

04:15.960 --> 04:16.960
Oh.

04:16.960 --> 04:19.640
No, but, yeah, there's a lot of good-looking women in Singapore.

04:19.640 --> 04:21.560
In Singapore, but not on board a ship.

04:21.560 --> 04:24.600
And how would you like to be nothing more than a sailor's salt-poor for more than a year?

04:24.600 --> 04:25.680
No, I wouldn't like that.

04:25.680 --> 04:26.960
No, I guess not.

04:26.960 --> 04:28.360
Well, you boys take care of yourselves.

04:28.360 --> 04:31.240
This is San Francisco. It isn't the Ponderosa.

04:31.240 --> 04:32.360
There's Hampton Johnny now.

04:32.360 --> 04:33.360
About time.

04:37.360 --> 04:42.240
Hopsing, I thought you were with your relatives.

04:42.240 --> 04:43.800
Something wrong, Hopsing?

04:43.800 --> 04:46.280
Not, no, for sure.

04:46.280 --> 04:49.360
Number three cousin, I see two cowboys going to Hopsing.

04:49.360 --> 04:51.480
Hit on head, not come up.

04:51.480 --> 04:53.560
Cousin, come quick, tell Hopsing.

04:53.560 --> 04:56.840
I think maybe it's Mr. Ham and Mr. Johnny.

04:56.840 --> 04:58.760
Hampton Johnny?

04:58.760 --> 04:59.400
Wait a minute.

04:59.400 --> 05:02.040
What makes you think it might be Hampton Johnny?

05:02.040 --> 05:06.560
They're not in hotel room.

05:06.560 --> 05:10.160
Well, maybe there's something I ought to check on.

05:10.160 --> 05:17.160
I think we'll all check it.

05:17.160 --> 05:25.520
Probably just covering some slip and having themselves a good time.

05:25.520 --> 05:30.000
Full off for midnight if you want to get paid.

05:30.000 --> 05:42.360
That'll be all, boys.

05:42.360 --> 05:46.560
Cowboys.

05:46.560 --> 05:58.120
What can I do to make them look more like cigarettes?

05:58.120 --> 06:08.880
Come on, boy, give us a heart.

06:08.880 --> 06:13.200
His mother out there.

06:13.200 --> 06:26.000
I'm gonna call the cops, and if they've taken it that way, rubber- artık.

06:26.000 --> 06:33.000
Are you the man in charge here?

06:35.600 --> 06:37.720
What can I do for you?

06:37.720 --> 06:43.000
My name is Ben Cockright. I just drove a herd of cattle across the Sierra.

06:43.000 --> 06:47.000
Well, San Francisco can certainly use a decent beef steak.

06:47.000 --> 06:52.000
Sergeant, I didn't come here to discuss beef steaks. Two of my top hands have disappeared.

06:52.000 --> 06:55.740
Well, it does happen.

06:55.740 --> 06:59.400
Is this the San Francisco Police Department?

06:59.400 --> 07:01.400
It's exactly that.

07:01.400 --> 07:06.120
Well, I just told you. Two of my top hands have disappeared and I've come here for help.

07:06.120 --> 07:09.600
And I suppose you expect me to drop everything and go find them.

07:09.600 --> 07:11.600
Yes, that's exactly it.

07:11.600 --> 07:15.600
Mr. Cockright, men are always disappearing in this city.

07:15.600 --> 07:18.680
You do nothing to try to find out what happened to them.

07:18.680 --> 07:24.880
Do you realize how many policemen it would take to keep an eye on every Shanghai hideout on the Barbary Coast?

07:24.880 --> 07:29.880
Well, Sergeant, I'm not interested in how many men it would take. I came here for help.

07:29.880 --> 07:34.880
Mr. Cockright, this is a steep point. Ships come here from all over the world. Ships need service.

07:34.880 --> 07:37.880
Oh, service is for not cowboys.

07:37.880 --> 07:40.880
You'd be surprised how many cowboys become sailors.

07:40.880 --> 07:45.880
I suggest that you do as all the ship captains do when they find themselves short-handed.

07:45.880 --> 07:49.880
Say, why don't you find yourself a new crew?

07:49.880 --> 07:54.880
Did you sit here and condone the violence that you've been seeing?

07:54.880 --> 08:00.880
I don't condone it, but I don't have enough men to do anything about it, so I accept it as an unfortunate fact.

08:00.880 --> 08:03.880
Now, please, if you'll excuse me.

08:03.880 --> 08:10.880
All right, Sergeant, you mark my words. I'm going to find those two men of mine with or without your help.

08:10.880 --> 08:20.880
All right, go right ahead. I'll find you. Look out.

08:20.880 --> 08:24.880
We're pretty close to the first thing.

08:24.880 --> 08:27.880
I'm not going to Shanghai. I'm going to Shanghai.

08:27.880 --> 08:29.880
Where'd you take him? Out on the desert?

08:29.880 --> 08:31.880
You keep talking about Shanghai.

08:31.880 --> 08:33.880
What was I doing?

08:33.880 --> 08:36.880
Half a journey around here, and I'm going to join.

08:36.880 --> 08:40.880
I see you're a bartender, but you don't seem to give out much information, do you?

08:40.880 --> 08:42.880
That's because they're all on coasts.

08:42.880 --> 08:45.880
Come on.

08:45.880 --> 08:47.880
I know.

08:47.880 --> 08:49.880
I'm going to get to the end of this one.

08:49.880 --> 08:51.880
Boss, why don't you come to that side of the street? I'll take this side.

08:51.880 --> 08:54.880
I'm saying go check with your cousins and see if they've seen anything.

08:54.880 --> 08:57.880
And I think it would be nice if you boys be out on the coast.

08:57.880 --> 08:59.880
You're as bad as a fall.

08:59.880 --> 09:02.880
Now, I heard the elementary kids had a lot of fun out here in this bar and club.

09:02.880 --> 09:05.880
You know what? I'd say the same thing.

09:05.880 --> 09:24.520
I don't believe that as a standards, you're going to play

09:24.520 --> 09:28.980
your role.

09:58.980 --> 10:02.980
Sonny, we swear we don't have drinks here, not information.

10:02.980 --> 10:03.980
Why?

10:03.980 --> 10:06.980
Just because you look too drunk.

10:06.980 --> 10:09.980
Why don't you get out of here?

10:09.980 --> 10:12.980
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

10:27.980 --> 10:30.980
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

10:30.980 --> 10:40.980
You'd better tell us.

10:45.980 --> 10:46.980
Mr. Cartwright?

10:46.980 --> 10:47.980
Yes, Mr. Cartwright.

10:47.980 --> 10:49.980
Where's Hoss and Joe?

10:49.980 --> 10:50.980
They go Farbley Coast.

10:50.980 --> 10:51.980
What?

10:51.980 --> 10:52.980
Not good.

10:52.980 --> 10:55.980
On Farbley Coast, hit, slice, cart, push.

10:55.980 --> 10:56.980
Very dangerous.

10:56.980 --> 10:57.980
To Shanghai.

10:57.980 --> 11:00.980
Little Joe didn't have enough sense to know that harsher word.

11:00.980 --> 11:01.980
What did you tell him?

11:01.980 --> 11:02.980
I tell him.

11:02.980 --> 11:03.980
He said he looked like fun.

11:03.980 --> 11:05.980
Looked like fun.

11:05.980 --> 11:08.980
Better find those two before they get into some real trouble.

11:08.980 --> 11:10.980
Farbley Coast.

11:10.980 --> 11:12.980
Hoss and go find Christian.

11:17.980 --> 11:18.980
You sir.

11:18.980 --> 11:23.980
You're a good man.

11:23.980 --> 11:24.980
You're a good man.

11:24.980 --> 11:26.980
I was your brother, I swear to heaven.

11:26.980 --> 11:29.980
I did not want you two to stay together.

11:29.980 --> 11:31.980
I can't get past this place.

11:31.980 --> 11:34.980
You're a good man.

11:34.980 --> 11:37.980
I'll let you go.

11:37.980 --> 11:39.980
Now, I swear to God.

11:39.980 --> 11:41.980
You're a good man.

11:41.980 --> 11:43.980
I'll let you go.

11:43.980 --> 11:48.980
Now, get in the car.

11:48.980 --> 11:50.980
All right.

11:59.980 --> 12:00.980
I'm sorry, great man.

12:00.980 --> 12:03.980
This haven't been in my favor.

12:03.980 --> 12:04.980
What?

12:04.980 --> 12:07.980
Eh, asshole, Carry your rifle back.

12:07.980 --> 12:11.980
Pass out on the roadway.

12:11.980 --> 12:14.980
I told you it was going to be fun down on this barbecue coast.

12:14.980 --> 12:15.980
Look at that, $100.

12:15.980 --> 12:19.980
Makes me mad in a mischief to think about how much talent I'd have wasted for free.

12:19.980 --> 12:21.980
Come on, Mr. Busthead, wake up.

12:24.980 --> 12:28.980
Mr. Busthead, like I told you, I don't want you chipping and chipping.

12:28.980 --> 12:30.980
I want myself to help.

12:34.980 --> 12:36.980
Mr. Busthead, I want you to meet my pa, Busthead.

12:36.980 --> 12:37.980
Bring this to me.

12:37.980 --> 12:38.980
My pa.

12:38.980 --> 12:39.980
Oh, yeah.

12:39.980 --> 12:41.980
Mr. Busthead.

12:41.980 --> 12:43.980
Sharon, what?

12:45.980 --> 12:47.980
Paul, you're a real fine fellow.

12:47.980 --> 12:53.980
Well, champ, if you have any conceivable idea of the seriousness of the situation we're in.

12:53.980 --> 12:54.980
Serious?

12:54.980 --> 12:56.980
Paul, you still think John and Hamper are in trouble?

12:56.980 --> 12:58.980
I don't think it. I know it.

12:58.980 --> 12:59.980
You mean Shane?

12:59.980 --> 13:00.980
Yes, I mean Shane.

13:00.980 --> 13:02.980
Dad, Bernie must tell this thing down at the bar.

13:02.980 --> 13:04.980
He wouldn't do no such thing.

13:04.980 --> 13:06.980
We're going to fight trouble unless it's forced on us.

13:06.980 --> 13:09.980
And that goes for you in particular.

13:09.980 --> 13:11.980
Don't stand there making a spectacle of yourself.

13:11.980 --> 13:12.980
Go get your coat.

13:12.980 --> 13:13.980
All right.

13:20.980 --> 13:22.980
Mr. Busthead, it's a real pleasure meeting you.

13:22.980 --> 13:24.980
You're going to be a great champion.

13:24.980 --> 13:29.980
Mr. Bust, Mr. Bust, you know, probably because he likes to talk to you.

13:29.980 --> 13:36.980
Mr. Bust, I'm very happy to see you. You're really strong. I've never seen anyone stronger than you.

13:36.980 --> 13:40.980
And if something pops up in your relatives' heads today, glad to meet you.

13:40.980 --> 13:43.980
Now, he will hunt down the bar.

13:43.980 --> 13:45.980
No, no, no, no, no, no.

13:45.980 --> 13:53.980
All right, because the questions everybody on Farbley Coast talk about men and two sons say they ask too many questions.

13:53.980 --> 13:55.980
Everybody's in a commutes.

13:55.980 --> 13:57.980
I don't see how we're going to find out anything.

13:57.980 --> 14:01.980
Well, we won't find out anything if the three of us keep barging in like we're going to tear the place apart.

14:01.980 --> 14:03.980
No, we used to do it that way.

14:03.980 --> 14:05.980
Well, it won't work now.

14:05.980 --> 14:07.980
You two boys should get back to the hotel and you stay there.

14:07.980 --> 14:10.980
Don't move until you hear from me. I'm going to see what I can find out alone.

14:10.980 --> 14:12.980
Hey, Paul, don't you think we're going with you?

14:12.980 --> 14:14.980
No, I don't.

14:14.980 --> 14:17.980
If I find out anything, I'll send Hopstein up there.

14:17.980 --> 14:19.980
Paul, you stay out of trouble, you hear?

14:19.980 --> 14:22.980
You make sure you listen to your own advice, young man.

14:22.980 --> 14:23.980
You too.

14:23.980 --> 14:24.980
Come on, Hopstein.

14:24.980 --> 14:27.980
I'll be right back.

14:27.980 --> 14:29.980
Don't worry about Paul.

14:29.980 --> 14:58.980
He's a beast.

14:59.980 --> 15:18.980
You boys wait here.

15:18.980 --> 15:20.980
I'm glad you're here.

15:20.980 --> 15:22.980
Thank you, Wayne.

15:22.980 --> 15:24.980
I'm trying to keep it up.

15:24.980 --> 15:29.980
If it isn't too much, Father, could you make me a brandy squash?

15:29.980 --> 15:40.980
Father, no, that's what I want.

15:40.980 --> 15:49.980
Thank you.

15:49.980 --> 15:51.980
Now, there's a surprise.

15:51.980 --> 15:53.980
What's the matter? Something wrong?

15:53.980 --> 15:57.980
Why, sir, this is the finest brandy squash I've ever tasted in my life.

15:57.980 --> 16:01.980
And I've tasted them all the way from New York to Chicago to New Orleans.

16:01.980 --> 16:03.980
Well, I'm glad you like it.

16:03.980 --> 16:07.980
It's an art, Artie. It's an art.

16:07.980 --> 16:11.980
Not many men have the talent for it.

16:11.980 --> 16:14.980
You've been working all alone, sir.

16:14.980 --> 16:17.980
Oh, can't say as I am.

16:17.980 --> 16:21.980
Why, a man with your talent could demand any of your guests.

16:21.980 --> 16:23.980
Yes, sir.

16:23.980 --> 16:25.980
I'm glad that you like it.

16:25.980 --> 16:28.980
And you've made a mighty lot of interesting people.

16:28.980 --> 16:30.980
All kinds. What about it?

16:30.980 --> 16:36.980
I have to tell you, that a place like this, practically everybody in town drops in here one time.

16:36.980 --> 16:39.980
Well, we get our share.

16:39.980 --> 16:41.980
I have two friends in town.

16:41.980 --> 16:48.980
I just got to go in here and show them what a good drink really tastes like.

16:48.980 --> 16:52.980
Say, hey, I wonder if they've been in here before.

16:52.980 --> 16:56.980
Well, I've got a pretty good memory for faces.

16:56.980 --> 17:00.980
A couple of cowboys, they work up a ranch in the Sierras.

17:00.980 --> 17:03.980
Don't know if I've heard of cowboys in town.

17:11.980 --> 17:13.980
Let's see now.

17:13.980 --> 17:15.980
I'm just saying. I want to get this straight.

17:15.980 --> 17:17.980
You said that they were two of them.

17:17.980 --> 17:19.980
That's right. Those two are inseparable.

17:19.980 --> 17:21.980
Two of the best guys I've ever had.

17:21.980 --> 17:25.980
My name is Alexander.

17:25.980 --> 17:28.980
I'm the proprietor of this establishment.

17:28.980 --> 17:33.980
I don't think I've had the pleasure of seeing you in here before.

17:33.980 --> 17:36.980
No, I have not.

17:36.980 --> 17:38.980
My name is Ben Cox.

17:38.980 --> 17:41.980
I'm the bar tender on the excellence of his drinks.

17:41.980 --> 17:44.980
Well, that's very kind of you.

17:44.980 --> 17:49.980
Why don't we go down to the end of the bar. It'll be quiet and more comfortable.

17:52.980 --> 17:54.980
Well, that's that.

17:54.980 --> 17:56.980
You said you were your own bar tender?

17:56.980 --> 17:59.980
Yes, Alexander Tender.

17:59.980 --> 18:01.980
Here's another drink.

18:01.980 --> 18:02.980
Thank you.

18:02.980 --> 18:03.980
Bar tender?

18:03.980 --> 18:06.980
It's a real squash this time.

18:06.980 --> 18:15.980
I'm not going to drink that for the bar.

18:15.980 --> 18:17.980
Well, I suppose you know what you're doing.

18:17.980 --> 18:21.980
Haven't you had enough trouble with those two cowboys you bought from Cutray Joe?

18:21.980 --> 18:24.980
That's their boss. You just dropped through the portal.

18:24.980 --> 18:27.980
I need three men to fill out Captain Shark's crew.

18:27.980 --> 18:31.980
And I don't prefer to buy them from Cutray Joe.

18:31.980 --> 18:35.980
And if you're thinking of asking me, please don't.

18:35.980 --> 18:40.980
I was laughing at you. You make the worst drinks in town.

18:54.980 --> 18:57.980
I'm getting worried. They've been going for an hour.

18:57.980 --> 18:58.980
Yeah.

18:58.980 --> 19:00.980
I'll tell you one thing, Joe.

19:00.980 --> 19:07.980
If you don't hear from Hop Sanger in the next 15 minutes, I'm just about ready to go down there and tear this dang Barbary Coast apart board for board.

19:15.980 --> 19:18.980
Mr. Paul, not sure.

19:18.980 --> 19:19.980
What do you mean you're not sure?

19:19.980 --> 19:21.980
What'd you learn?

19:21.980 --> 19:23.980
Mr. Kotlite told Hop Sanger to wait.

19:23.980 --> 19:25.980
Hop Sanger waited a long time.

19:25.980 --> 19:27.980
Mr. Kotlite will come back.

19:27.980 --> 19:30.980
Hop Sanger waited? Come see who?

19:30.980 --> 19:35.980
Hop Sanger, you shouldn't have done that. Paul comes out of there and you ain't there. What's he gonna do?

19:35.980 --> 19:37.980
Number five hasn't waited.

19:37.980 --> 19:39.980
Well, there's nothing wrong with Paul.

19:39.980 --> 20:08.980
Well, you can take care of himself.

20:08.980 --> 20:11.980
Boss, Mr. Kotlite.

20:11.980 --> 20:13.980
Johnny, you boys are...

20:13.980 --> 20:15.980
How did they get you in here?

20:15.980 --> 20:17.980
You'd never believe it.

20:17.980 --> 20:19.980
After me telling the boys to stay out of trouble.

20:19.980 --> 20:21.980
I know, Joe.

20:21.980 --> 20:25.980
